      "message": "fix(post): refuse a Tormach move with no A word in an indexed operation\n\nA rapid or linear record with no A word read as tool angle 0. Inside an\noperation indexed away from A0, the post (since #2386) then turned A back\nto 0 with a G0/G1 A0 block, which swings the part under the tool. The\nstream means \"keep the pose\" for a move with no axis (post::dump), and\nstates a real turn to upright with an explicit A0. indexFor now refuses\nsuch a record by name and does not write it.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/tormach_no_a_word.rs.\n\nFixes #2473\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
